<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Horinger</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Helingeer</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Horinger is a county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohhot">Hohhot</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-mongolia">Inner Mongolia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, south of the city. It contains the ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shengle">Shengle</a>, the early capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuoba">Tuoba</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a>, and an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Eastern Han</a> tomb whose wall paintings show official life and farming on the northern frontier of China in the 2nd century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/horinger.jpg" alt="Horinger" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: wanghongliu · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2004%E5%B9%B4_%E8%92%99%E7%89%9B%E4%B9%B3%E4%B8%9A%E9%9B%86%E5%9B%A2_Mengniu_Dairy_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
